    "terrainName": "bt-range",
    "description": "What: the ground-shaping tools on a FLAT terrain (bt-range has no height grid, only groundZ): a 2 m 'Raise' area (x 20-50, y 10-40), a 1 m 'Lower' area (x 80-110, y 10-40) and a 'Ditch' line drawn across the whole range at y = 60; a rifleman is ordered onto the raised ground, one into the hollow and one down into the ditch, and a car is ordered across the ditch. Judge: (1) Hill Rifle ends standing about 2 m up; (2) Hollow Rifle ends about 1 m down; (3) Ditch Rifle ends about 1 m down in the ditch; (4) the car never crosses the ditch (a ditch keeps vehicles out) and ends south of it. Fail: either man stands at 0 m (the shape did not carve the ground - CE-1963 / CE-1964) or the car drives across."
  },
